  "description": "Custom dashboard for kube-state-metrics. The project ships no dashboard of its own; panels use only the standard kube_* families from its own documentation (kube_pod_status_phase, kube_deployment_status/spec_replicas, kube_pod_container_resource_requests/limits, kube_persistentvolumeclaim_status_phase, kube_node_status_allocatable, kube_job_status_*, kube_statefulset_status_replicas). Series are matched by the scrape job (the Target Allocator names it kube-state-metrics/kube-state-metrics) because kube_* series carry the TARGET object's namespace label, not kube-state-metrics' own; the $namespace variable drills into per-namespace breakdowns. Datasource hardcoded to the in-cluster victoriametrics uid.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "last"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "victoriametrics"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (phase) (kube_pod_status_phase{job=~\".*kube-state-metrics.*\", namespace=~\"$namespace\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{phase}}"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Pods by phase",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
